From df85ed7efbb8ad7cd8cb77923624bce3ad1b5474 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:28:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(post): add RichAuto DSP A11 3-axis router post

Add assets/posts/richauto.cps and register it as "RichAuto DSP A11".
The output follows the .mmg program that a Laguna Swift A11 runs (#1907):
N10 step-10 sequence numbers, no spaces between words, three decimals,
G00/G1, M03S<rpm>, modal words left out, and a final % line.

The post writes G21G90G17 and no G54 (the pendant work origin). It keeps
one tool per program, expands drilling to plain moves, writes incremental
I/J/K arcs, and refuses tapping, G41/G42, probing, rotary moves, a second
tool and other work offsets by name.

Pinned by script_richauto (41 tests) and the conformance matrix.

Fixes #1914

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
